# 5. There is an even more serious anti-theatre violation

Look at these defaults:

```python
TYPE_DEFAULTS = {
    "work": {
        "epistemic_ceiling": "SCHOLARLY_CORROBORATED",
        ...
    },
    "passage": {
        "epistemic_ceiling": "SCHOLARLY_CORROBORATED",
        ...
    },
}
```

A thing does not become scholarly corroborated because its object type is `work`.

This conflicts directly with Pāṭala's strongest doctrine.

Pāṭala's README says:

> a tested schema ≠ a result; only independent gold + blind eval + metric + human adjudication makes something real.

Therefore:

```text
object TYPE
≠
epistemic STATE
```

Canonical default should probably be:

```text
SOURCE object:
    provenance_verified = true/false

epistemic claim:
    MACHINE_PROPOSED initially

review:
    independently advanced
```

A source can be authentically a scholarly publication without every proposition reconstructed from it becoming `SCHOLARLY_CORROBORATED`.

This distinction is foundational.

