# 7. `review.py` contains the right architectural primitive

The actual shape of this is good.

You have:

```text
state
+
event/evidence
→ deterministic reducer
→ next state
```

rather than agents directly setting status.

That should absolutely survive.

This is one of the most important architectures in the entire system.

Agents should never be allowed to do:

```python
object.status = "VERIFIED"
```

Instead:

```text
Agent produces ReviewEvent
       ↓
event appended
       ↓
Reducer
       ↓
state calculated deterministically
```

The canonical pattern should be:

```text
OBJECT
immutable identity/content revision

EVENT LOG
append-only observations/actions

REDUCER
deterministic current-state computation

PROJECTION
materialized current state

GATE
predicate permitting next transition
```

This is where herdr + Arcan + your own factory converge.

