# 20. The performance CI should be brutal

I would establish explicit budgets.

### Human reading

```text
ordinary page JS              0 KB target
interactive page JS           bounded island only
compressed HTML               <100 KB typical
CLS                           ~0
cached page origin work       0
```

The existing performance spec proposes essentially these bounds.

### Agent

```text
resolve                  1 request
context                  1 request
compare                  1 request
trace                    1 request

default context          <= 4k tokens
standard deep context    <= 8k
graph depth              <= 2 default
```

### Factory

```text
changing one passage MUST NOT rebuild one work
changing one work MUST NOT rebuild entire corpus
```

And CI should verify this.

For a fixture graph:

```text
mutate node P23
expected invalidated = {T23,C23,A4,E2,Q6,Q7}
actual invalidated   = ...
```

Mismatch = test failure.

